\section{Proposed research idea}

\subsection{Context}

The research plan builds on STraM in two work packages:

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{WP1} keeps STraM's two-stage structure and mean--CVaR
        objective but makes disruptions the uncertainty and a response model
        the recourse. It uses the value of the stochastic solution as its
        benchmark, as STraM does.
  \item \textbf{WP2} replaces the recourse model by machine-learning
        surrogates, either embedded as constraints or used to generate
        candidate cuts.
\end{itemize}


Both depend on being able to run, inspect and change STraM. The published
code needs Gurobi, and Gurobi's free academic licence needs a university
affiliation, which is not available at this stage.

\subsection{Questions the work set out to answer}

\begin{enumerate}
  \item Can STraM be run with a free solver, and how much code must change?
  \item Does the free solver reproduce the published results?
  \item Does it scale to the nine-scenario model used in the paper?
  \item Is STraM therefore a workable base for the surrogate research?
\end{enumerate}

