Guidance and expectations that proved wrong during the session:

\begin{itemize}
  \item The plan said to remove the \texttt{warmstart},
        \texttt{symbolic\_solver\_labels} and \texttt{keepfiles} arguments by
        hand. Testing showed HiGHS accepts them; the real problems were the
        Gurobi option names and \texttt{results.solver.time}.
  \item The reference value 2300.12 was taken from a log that predates the
        current data. It should not have been used.
  \item The emission cap setting was first left on. It was switched off so
        that runs correspond to the reference logs.
  \item Before Run 4 the stochastic objective was expected to be 1--2\%
        above the Gurobi value, by extrapolation from Run 2. It was 18\%
        above. The extrapolation did not allow for how far the Gurobi
        solution of the larger model departs from feasibility.
\end{itemize}

\section{Updated installation procedure}
\label{sec:install}

This replaces the steps in the STraM README for a Windows machine using Git
Bash and no Gurobi licence.

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Install Python 3.10.11.} Download the ``Windows installer
        (64-bit)'' from
        \url{https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-31011/} and tick
        ``Add python.exe to PATH''. Later 3.10 releases are source-only.
  \item \textbf{Confirm it is visible.}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
py -0p
\end{lstlisting}
  \item \textbf{Clone the repository} (about 640 MB).
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
git clone https://github.com/ntnuiotenergy/STraM
cd STraM
\end{lstlisting}
  \item \textbf{Create and activate the environment with 3.10.}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
py -3.10 -m venv env
source env/Scripts/activate
python --version        # must print Python 3.10.11
\end{lstlisting}
  \item \textbf{Install the packages.}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install highspy typing_extensions
python -c "import highspy; print('highspy OK')"
\end{lstlisting}
  \item \textbf{Apply the code changes} in Section~\ref{sec:changes}.
  \item \textbf{Keep copies of the reference logs and result files}, because
        runs overwrite them.
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
mkdir Data/Output/reference
cp Data/Output/*_logfile.log Data/Output/*_results.pickle Data/Output/reference/
\end{lstlisting}
  \item \textbf{Run.}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
python Main.py
\end{lstlisting}
\end{enumerate}

The activation command depends on the terminal:
\texttt{source env/Scripts/activate} in Git Bash,
\texttt{env\textbackslash Scripts\textbackslash activate} in Command Prompt,
and \texttt{.\textbackslash env\textbackslash Scripts\textbackslash
Activate.ps1} in PowerShell. Overwritten files can also be restored with
\texttt{git checkout -{}- Data/Output/}.

\section{Code changes}
\label{sec:changes}

\subsection{\texttt{Model.py}: solver call}

The function \texttt{solve\_model()} at the end of the file was replaced. It
is the only place where the solver is called.

\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python]
    def solve_model(self, warmstart=False,
                    FeasTol=(10**(-2)),
                    MIP_gap=MIPGAP,
                    TimeLimit=None,   # seconds. None = no limit
                    num_focus=0,      # Gurobi-only (ignored)
                    Crossover=-1,     # Gurobi-only (ignored)
                    Method=-1,        # Gurobi-only (ignored)
                    NodeMethod=-1):   # Gurobi-only (ignored)

        import time as _time

        opt = pyomo.opt.SolverFactory('appsi_highs')
        if not opt.available():
            raise Exception("HiGHS is not available. Run: pip install highspy")

        opt.options['mip_rel_gap'] = MIP_gap
        opt.options['primal_feasibility_tolerance'] = FeasTol
        if TimeLimit is not None:
            opt.options['time_limit'] = float(TimeLimit)

        start = _time.time()
        try:
            results = opt.solve(self.model, tee=True)
        except RuntimeError as err:
            log_infeasible_constraints(self.model)
            raise Exception('HiGHS did not return a feasible solution: '
                            + str(err))
        solve_time = _time.time() - start

        solver_stat = results.solver.status
        termination_cond = results.solver.termination_condition
        if (solver_stat == pyomo.opt.SolverStatus.ok) and (
                termination_cond == pyomo.opt.TerminationCondition.optimal):
            print('the solution is feasible and optimal')
        else:
            log_infeasible_constraints(self.model)
            log_infeasible_constraints(self.model, log_expression=True,
                                       log_variables=True)
            logging.basicConfig(filename='example.log', encoding='utf-8',
                                level=logging.INFO)
            raise Exception('Solver Status: ', solver_stat,
                            'Termination Condition: ', termination_cond)

        print('Solution time: ' + str(solve_time))
\end{lstlisting}

