\subsubsection*{Conclusion}

The HiGHS result is consistent with the bound; the published value is not.
The published stochastic-programme objective belongs to a solution that
leaves 8--12\% of demand unserved. This follows from the authors' own files
and does not depend on HiGHS. An earlier test on the EV model pointed the
same way: allowing variables to fall $10^{-4}$ below zero lowers its
objective by 3.1\%, and $10^{-3}$ lowers it by 24.8\%.

\subsection{The value of the stochastic solution}
\label{sec:vss}

The value of the stochastic solution (VSS) is the EEV objective minus the SP
objective: what is gained by planning with scenarios instead of expected
values.

