\section{Achievement}

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Independence from a commercial licence.} STraM runs on a
        fully open stack (Python, Pyomo, HiGHS) with changes to one function
        and one name.
  \item \textbf{A documented, repeatable installation} for Windows that
        works with current package versions.
  \item \textbf{Every model in the paper's base case solved to optimality},
        from 16 thousand to 4.48 million constraints, including the full
        stochastic programme in about 14 minutes of wall time.
  \item \textbf{A reproducibility finding on the published results}: the
        stochastic-programme objective and the value of the stochastic
        solution depend on a loose feasibility tolerance, shown from the
        authors' own solution files and an independent bound.
  \item \textbf{A minor code finding}: the misplaced argument in the EV
        stage, with its effect measured.
  \item \textbf{Measured costs per model evaluation}: 20--27 seconds for a
        one-scenario model, 12 minutes for nine scenarios with the first
        stage fixed, and 14 minutes for the full stochastic programme.
\end{enumerate}

